WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
Austin tonight, Elon

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.135
Musk banning

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.370
multiple tech journalists

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.538
from Twitter with no explanation.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.107
The suspensions come just hours

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:07.607
after Twitter

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.675
shut down an account

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.476
belonging to

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.611
an emerging competitor, Mastodon.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.312
The ban includes

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.014
The New York Times's Ryan Mack,

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.048
The Washington Post's

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.116
Drew Harwell,

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.585
and our own CNN's Donie O'Sullivan.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.053
Here with me to talk about all this,

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.321
we have John Berman.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.089
Also Tony O'Sullivan

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.357
and CNN's Oliver Dorsey.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.760
What did you do that was so bad, Tony?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.795
We reported on Elon Musk.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.930
We were talking about the world's well,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.564
formally the world's

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.767
richest man, world's second richest man

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.235
who runs Twitter.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.437
He has taken particular

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.773
a hybrid.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.340
Yes.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.174
He's been annoyed

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.275
that there has been this account,

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.810
which has been active for years now,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.645
which tracks the movements

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.047
of his private jet. Right.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:47.981
But you're not doing that.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.649
Why didn't you get banned?

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.184
So we reported how yesterday

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:52.652
he shut that account down.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.554
And tonight we continued to report on it.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.923
He is claiming on social media that

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.426
I and other journalists

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.860
shared the precise

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.796
live location of his jets.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.363
And therefore,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.397
that's why he kicked us off,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.665
because we cause danger to him.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.534
Certainly my case, I didn't

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.869
we we just posted

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.971
stories about what was happening,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.907
him shutting down those accounts.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.543
But, look, I think the bigger issue here

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.077
is, of course,

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.578
this is supposed to be the guy

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.914
who's the free speech absolutist. Right.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.614
Are you saying

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.916
that Elon Musk is saying

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.651
something that isn't true?

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.820
I think that seems to be the case.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.454
I mean,

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.822
it goes actually goes

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:29.689
further than that, John.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.958
He's he was touting,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.427
I mean, freedom of speech as this beacon.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:34.928
That Twitter

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.296
would be a beacon of that

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.530
until it comes to anybody

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:37.931
saying something

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.466
about something he doesn't like.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.634
There's a word for that democracy.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.303
It might be called hypocrisy.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:43.503
Yeah.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.604
Look, first of all,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.438
Elon Musk's

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.806
understanding of freedom of speech

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.941
has always been somewhat limited.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:48.641
There's no

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.810
constitutional freedom of speech

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.078
for a private company.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.046
Never has been.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:53.947
And as far as I know,

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:54.881
there never will be.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.583
So his criticisms of Twitter

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.251
from before were off base

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.085
It's his company.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:02.555
I mean, he can ban Dhoni if he wants to.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.291
It's just wildly hypocritical.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:05.558
Oliver,

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.060
what is CNN going to do about this?

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.761
Well, I think this raises a big question

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.362
about what

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.396
the free press,

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:10.864
what the future

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:13.533
of the free press on Twitter looks like.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:13.900
You know,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.101
our news organizations

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.202
are going to stand by

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.837
as the reporters are just

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.371
you know,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.473
hastily banned without explanation.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.242
CNN is saying it's

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.377
going to reevaluate its relationship

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.012
with Twitter based on the response

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:26.346
it gets.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:26.913
I want to read you

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.815
the full statement Alison. It says,

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.485
The impulsive and unjustified

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.354
suspension of a number of reporters,

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.822
including CNN's Donie

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.357
O'Sullivan, is concerning

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.691
but not surprising.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.893
And it goes on to say, Twitter's

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.628
increasing instability

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.697
and volatility, volatility should have

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.266
should be of incredible concern

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.168
for everyone who uses Twitter.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.235
And then it goes on to say,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.204
we have asked Twitter for an explanation

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.673
and we will reevaluate our relationship

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.141
based on that response.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:55.942
And I think it's so important

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:56.342
to point out

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.977
that Twitter really needs

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:00.480
are really relies on news.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:00.947
I mean, that's

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:01.581
what's kind

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.249
of the lifeblood of journalists.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.951
I mean, they're all on Twitter.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.251
And so

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.686
if you see news organizations

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.988
start to pull their reporters,

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.523
pull their brand accounts,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.525
pull their content off of Twitter,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:12.992
you know,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.493
that's going to be

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.794
a real blow to the platform

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.563
and make it less usable

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.697
I think, for the average person

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.631
doing my job here.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.566
And to play

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.834
devil's advocate against myself, I guess.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.837
Look, when Trump got suspended,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:25.805
everybody pointed out

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.440
that that was also, you know,

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.208
a concerning thing

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.576
for many people kicking off the

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.810
then president of the United States,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.612
regardless of the circumstances.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.781
But, you know, I have a platform.

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:36.716
I'm here talking to you on CNN.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.218
There are other social media platforms.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.319
The First Amendment,

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.853
despite what Musk

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.688
and a lot of his supporters

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.924
say, does not actually apply to Twitter.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.859
I think what is more concerning

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.095
here, though, is independent journalist,

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.230
freelance journalist

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.164
all around the world,

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.298
many of whom are covering

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.967
maybe abuses and ongoing,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.402
that Musk's other companies Tesla Space

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.204
X, think about the chilling effect

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.206
that might have because as Oliver said,

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.040
many journalists

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.609
rely on Twitter to get their work out

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.343
there, particularly

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.911
if they are independent freelancers.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.445
But furthermore,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.546
one of the things that I think

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.847
where the hypocrisy comes in

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.849
is that a lot of people felt that

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.884
hateful, vitriolic, violent speech

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.685
shouldn't be allowed on there

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.020
because of personal safety.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.054
Elon Musk doesn't

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.923
want his personal safety violated.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.857
I mean, that's what it comes down to.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:18.891
He doesn't want people to know

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.759
where he is.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.593
It's not personal safety

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.195
when it's about him.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.997
He doesn't like it so much.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.366
Look, I I said this before you.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.133
Elon Musk

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.768
is a very successful businessman.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:29.969
He's a rich guy.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:30.837
He's a rich guy

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.071
who bought a media company.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.606
But because he bought a media company

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.109
doesn't mean he understands a thing

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.611
about the media business

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.912
or about how this all works.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.748
And I think he's just proving that again

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.116
and again and again.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.851
If I basically think we should say that

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:46.886
he is actively smearing people

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:47.720
like don't saying

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.888
that they effectively posted

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.890
assassination coordinates on him

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.458
for reporting on this Elon

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.661
jet account, that's obviously not true.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:55.561
Totally false.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.763
But that's why you're hearing him

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.331
say on Twitter tonight.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:04:59.899
Also, the location of his address

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.501
is publicly available information.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.069
Yeah. Wow.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.438
I mean, that again, it's all been right.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.406
Don't you have to be careful?

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.074
Always bring us down with you here.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.142
I always thought I get banned for

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:09.809
my bad jokes.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.577
But no, that really adds

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.645
another wrinkle to it.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.113
Gentlemen, thank you very much.

